  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cool and dry weather continues through the weekend,\nalthough a slow-moving Nor'easter off the coast will bring gusty\nwinds along the Chesapeake Bay and minor tidal flooding at times\nthrough Friday.\n\nSurface high pressure remains over the forecast area through  \nthe forecast period as a Nor'easter continues to drift offshore.\nA tight pressure gradient between surface high pressure nearby\nand the offshore Nor'easter will yield gusty conditions daily, \nmainly along and east of the I-95 corridor. Under high pressure,\ntemperatures moderate through Thursday with high temperatures \nin the 50s and 60s. Overnight low temperatures will be in the \n30s and 40s through Thursday night. Aloft, upper level troughing\ndevelops across the eastern CONUS as ridging develops over \ncentral CONUS. By Thursday, the Nor'easter is absorbed into the \nupper trough and tracks off the coast of New England. \n\nSurface high pressure builds southward out of southeastern\nCanada and eastern Great Lakes regions into the mid-Atlantic\nFriday through Monday. Dry conditions are expected each day with\na gradual moderating trend in temperatures.",
